1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,620
Is there a hole in your eye?

2
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:05,990
Cover your left eye with your hand

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:09,060
With your right eye, look only at the cross (+)

4
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:14,830
Bring your face close to the screen,
then slowly move back

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:19,830
Keep your eye on the cross (+)!

6
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:22,300
Did the red dot vanish?

7
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:24,770
If not, try changing the distance a little

8
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:26,470
Let's slice the eye and look from above

9
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:28,120
The inner wall is packed
with cells that sense light

10
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:30,820
Their nerves gather in one spot
and leave the eye

11
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:32,890
Light from the cross (+) lands on cells

12
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:35,890
Light from the red dot lands
right on the nerve's exit

13
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:38,160
There are no light-sensing cells here,
so the light can't be felt

14
00:00:38,210 --> 00:00:41,530
This spot is the blind spot!

15
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:44,000
So why don't we normally notice?

16
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:46,570
Each eye's gap is in a different place,
so the other eye covers it

17
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:52,140
With one eye open?
Your brain fills it in with the surroundings

18
00:00:52,190 --> 00:00:54,490
Everyone has one in each eye

19
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:58,290
NEXT: Stare at red, then look at a white wall…
